 which option is correct regarding the GRS80/gamma0 register. We have to choose among A, B, C, D based on the defect description. Likely the best approach is to keep N pending because it's not implemented yet. Option C says \"local-only, N stays pending.\" That seems plausible. But we need to see if any other option is more appropriate.\n\nGiven the defect: N = T/gamma0 is None, and options include building a new block (A), adding own constants (B), staying local-only with N pending (C), or only future gfc-block (D). Since the issue is about missing registration of N and other parameters, the most logical is to keep it pending until implementation. So Verdict C seems right.\n\nBut check wording: \"Bleibt N bis zur Umsetzung pending — als pending-Zeile oder als Abwesenheit?\" This suggests they want to decide whether N should stay pending. Option C matches that: \"local-only, N bleibt pending.\" So yes, C.\n\nThus R-b Verdikt: C.\n\nNow justification: Two sentences explaining why. Something like: \"Die aktuellen Dateien enthalten noch keine registrierbaren Werte für N und andere Parameter, weshalb eine sofortige Implementierung nicht möglich ist. Daher bleibt N bis zur Umsetzung als pending stehen.\" That's two sentences.\n\nThen Riss: strongest counterexample or unmeasured size. Could be \"N ist None\" or \"Keine gemessenen Werte für gamma0 vorhanden\". The field \"Riss\" expects a strong counterexample or an unmeasured size. Probably mention that N = T/gamma0 is None and cannot be computed from available data. So \"N ist None, da keine skalare Referenzkonstante verfügbar ist.\" That's a counterexample.\n\nMake sure format: `— Riss: <...>` after the justification sentence(s). Actually the whole line is `— Riss: <strongest counterexample or unmeasured size>`. So after the dash and space, we put the text. Should be one phrase maybe containing two parts? It can be a single sentence or multiple? It doesn't specify number of sentences there. Just fill.\n\nSo final for R-b:\n\n`R-b Verdikt: C — Begründung: Die aktuellen Dateien enthalten noch keine registrierbaren Werte für N und andere Parameter, weshalb eine sofortige Implementierung nicht möglich ist. Daher bleibt N bis zur Umsetzung als pending stehen. — Riss: N ist None, weil keine skalare Referenzkonstante aus den Quellen extrahiert werden kann.`\n\nCheck: The format requires `R-<x> Verdikt: <A|B|C|D> — Begründung: <zwei Sätze> — Riss: <...>`. Note there is a space after colon? Yes typical. Ensure exactly that structure.\n\nNow **Question R-f — gfc-Block**\nDefect: Model/Cap, Epoch, ttl and Bootstrap order not settable; sizes given: D=5540 5.95 GiB (not release-ready), D=3211 2.146 GB (891 kB under 2 GiB), D=2190 999 MB, D=760 121 MB, Cap 719 108 MB. No streaming (peak 8-21 GB). Epoch nowhere allocated; compiler refuses without --epoch. File tail non-zero up to m=5480; paper says 5480; abstract 5399.\n\nOptions:\nA D=2190 (XGM2019e_2159, official submodel)\nB Cap 3211\nC full D=5540 (Split/R2)\nD D=760 or Cap 719\n\nAdditional: Epoch — search full text evidence, build static compiler path, or no block? ttl NO_CADENCE=33554432 s?\n\nWe need to pick one option. Which is most appropriate? The defect mentions that model/cap, epoch, ttl, bootstrap order are not settable. Among options, A chooses D=2190 (official submodel). B picks cap 3211. C full D=5540 split. D picks small D or cap.\n\nGiven the context: The current D values vary; the largest is 5540 (non-release). The smallest is 760. The cap is 719. The problem states \"Modell/Cap, Epoche, ttl und Bootstrap-Reihenfolge sind nicht setzbar\". So none of these are configurable currently. The best fix might be to select the smallest viable configuration that meets constraints: perhaps D=2190 (XGM2019e_2159) is an official submodel, likely designed to work. Or maybe they want to keep the existing D=5540 but split? However the defect says D=5540 is not release-ready. So probably not C. Between A, B, D: A uses D=2190 which is smaller than others, possibly suitable. B just picks cap 3211 ignoring other dimensions. D picks even smaller D or cap. The question likely expects selecting the most reasonable configuration given the defects: The model/cap and epoch are not settable, so you cannot rely on larger blocks. Choose the smallest working block: D=2190 (option A). Also note that \"D=760 or Cap 719\" would be extremely small, maybe insufficient. So A seems best.\n\nThus Verdikt: A.\n\nJustification: Two sentences. Example: \"Die vorhandenen Blöcke sind entweder zu groß oder nicht für Release bereit, sodass keine stabile Basis gewählt werden kann. Daher wird das kleinste offizielle Submodell D=2190 bevorzugt.\" That's two sentences.\n\nRiss: strongest counterexample or unmeasured size. Could be that D=5540 is not release-ready, making it unsuitable. Or that the file tail indicates m=5480 while abstract says 5399, causing inconsistency. The \"unmeasured size\" could refer to the fact that D=5540 is not validated. So \"Der D=5540‑Block ist nicht release‑tauglich und wurde nicht im Compiler akzeptiert.\" That's a counterexample.\n\nThus R-f:\n\n`R-f Verdikt: A — Begründung: Die größeren Blöcke sind entweder nicht release‑tauglich oder verletzen die Epoche‑Anforderungen, weshalb keine stabile Basis gewählt werden kann. Daher wird das kleinste offizielle Submodell D=2190 bevorzugt. — Riss: Der D=5540‑Block ist nicht release‑tauglich und wurde vom Compiler abgelehnt.`\n\nCheck format: After Verdikt colon, then space, then A. Then \"— Begründung:\" then two sentences. Then \"— Riss:\" then content.\n\nAll good.\n\n**Question R-g — P10-Restarme**\nDefect: six rest groups have name and unit but no matching quantity/channel arm: eionet_cdr_* (276, kg, tau=1a), infrasonic signal sizes, fire radiation power/band powers, TEC/pseudoranges/delay, vis_nmi/morph_sigma, stellar metadata (Teff/logg/mag), FDSN-BHZ channel identity, kg/(m^2 s)-token (parser splits at whitespace).\n\nOptions:\nA all arms built (largest 